{"schema":2,"commit":"9650beb5d1430cea72453d607f0c470ab22d87d3","branch":"fix/copilot-hook-version-agnostic","base_sha":"fbc70d665933c444c03a2a36991ea693c42f1c22","message":"Credit Copilot agent-runtime edits whatever shape the hook payload takes\n\nCopilot for JetBrains 1.18+, the Copilot CLI and VS Code's Copilot SDK\nsessions all run the copilot-agent runtime. Its hooks send camelCase\nfields (toolName, toolArgs, sessionId), batch pre-hook calls as\ntoolCalls[{name, args}], and name tools edit/view/powershell with\npath/old_str/new_str. The Copilot hook read none of it: edit-tool\nchanges recorded nothing and were committed as Human, and a powershell\nedit had no pre-baseline, so every uncommitted line was credited to\nCopilot.\n\nparseHookEnvelope reads the envelope tolerantly (snake/camel spellings,\nargs as object or JSON string, every call in a batch) and is used by\nboth `record copilot` and `record --pre`. A call whose payload names\nno file and is not a known read tool falls back to the shell disk-diff\npath, and the pre-hook now takes the repo baseline for any such call,\nnot only for shell tool names. powershell/pwsh count as shells; grep,\nglob, ask_user and similar read tools are skipped.\n\nUnrecognised payloads are tallied in ~/.blamely/hook_drift.json (tool\nname and top-level key names only, never values); `blamely doctor`\nwarns when one was seen in the last 14 days and a successful\n`blamely update` clears the tally.","coding_time_nanos":10253371245000,"totals":{"added_lines":912,"ai_added_lines":912,"human_added_lines":0,"deleted_lines":106,"ai_deleted_lines":62,"human_deleted_lines":44,"files":12,"tokens":{"input":38,"output":39212,"cache_read":4078973,"cache_write":36438},"models":{"claude-opus-5-5":912}},"by_tool":{"claude":{"lines":912,"deleted_lines":62,"suggested_lines":3695,"accepted_lines":912,"tokens":{"input":38,"output":39212,"cache_read":4078973,"cache_write":36438}}},"by_gen_type":{"chat":974,"cli":0,"completion":0,"human":44},"file